# Comma-separated list of allowed parent-frame origins. The published SDK's
# IframeTransport drops every inbound postMessage whose `event.origin` isn't in
# this list AND refuses to mount (throws -> blank screen) if the list is empty.
# The value is BAKED IN AT BUILD TIME (import.meta.env), so it must be correct
# for the environment the bundle is served in.
#
# Production (.env.production): LOCAL `vite build` only. The platform's build
# sets this variable itself, which overrides the .env files.
#   VITE_BLOCK_ALLOWED_PARENT_ORIGINS={{ civitaiParentOriginsCSV }},https://www.civitai.com
#
# Local harness (.env.development): the dev-server origin. `npm run dev:harness`
# serves on localhost:5186 and fires BLOCK_INIT from window.location.origin.
# `npm run dev:tunnel` + `civitai app dev-tunnel` additionally embed this dev
# server inside the REAL host at /apps/dev/<id> on any Civitai domain, so the dev
# allowlist also carries every one (DEV-ONLY — production is unaffected).
#   VITE_BLOCK_ALLOWED_PARENT_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5186,{{ civitaiParentOriginsCSV }}

# Set to "true" to mount the dev Harness. `npm run dev:harness` / `dev:live`
# flip this on. NEVER set it in a production build.
VITE_DEV_HARNESS=

# Which harness to mount: "mock" (default) or "live".
#   mock  -> the SDK MOCK host: synthetic, no real Buzz, no compute. Its result
#            image is fetched from the third-party host placehold.co (blocked
#            -> a broken image under a Done status).
#            `npm run dev:harness` sets this.
#   live  -> the SDK LIVE host (`createLiveHost`): forwards the protocol to the
#            REAL Civitai backend with a REAL block token (spends REAL Buzz /
#            real compute). `npm run dev:live` sets this. With no
#            VITE_LIVE_BLOCK_TOKEN it FAILS SAFE (renders a notice, never spends).
VITE_HARNESS_MODE=

# LIVE mode only. A short-lived (~4h), scoped dev block token minted for local
# dev via the invite-gated dev-token endpoint (POST /api/v1/blocks/dev-token).
#
# ⚠️ DEV-ONLY SECRET THAT SPENDS REAL BUZZ — put the real value in the
# git-ignored `.env.development.local`, NEVER here and NEVER committed.
# NEVER HERE IS ABOUT THE UPLOAD, NOT JUST GIT: `civitai app submit` packages
# THIS FILE verbatim (`.env.example` is one of three allow-listed dotenv names)
# and ships it to the platform and to a human moderator reviewer — a token
# pasted here reaches them even if git never sees it. It would not even work:
# vite reads `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.[mode]` and `.env.[mode].local`, never
# `.env.example`, so `dev:live` would still fail safe while the token travelled.
# The CLI writes the right file for you:
#   civitai app dev-token <your-app-slug> --env >> .env.development.local
#
# The mint accepts a PENDING (un-approved) slug — right after `civitai app submit`
# it returns 200 with appId: pending-pubreq_… , so you can dev:live-test before
# approval (no need to wait for approval + deploy).
#
# REAL generation (spends real Buzz) needs TWO things:
#   1. A credential that carries AI Services. Either opt in on the browser login
#      with `civitai login --scopes generate` (additive — you keep Apps submit),
#      or store a full-scope PERSONAL API KEY (create at
#      https://civitai.com/user/account) with `civitai login --token <key>`.
#      A DEFAULT `civitai login` deliberately does NOT carry AI Services, so the
#      server strips `ai:write:budgeted` from what it mints: viewer + catalog
#      work, but estimate -> submit -> spend does NOT.
#   2. An explicit spend request on the mint: the CLI never asks for budgeted
#      spend implicitly, so pass --spend:
#        civitai app dev-token <your-app-slug> --spend --env >> .env.development.local
# Confirm your credential with `civitai whoami`.
# Storage does NOT work under dev:live with any token (see README, "Live v1 scope").
# See README. Leave the line below EMPTY — it documents the name, nothing more.
#   VITE_LIVE_BLOCK_TOKEN=<the minted token>   # in .env.development.local only
VITE_LIVE_BLOCK_TOKEN=

# LIVE mode only. The TARGET the vite dev proxy forwards backend calls to.
# `dev:live` routes the live host's `/api/...` calls through the vite dev server
# SAME-ORIGIN (localhost:5186) — no CORS preflight, and the proxy rewrites the
# Origin header to an allowlisted host so civitai's tRPC origin gate accepts it.
# The browser never fetches civitai.com directly. This overrides the proxy
# target only; defaults to https://civitai.com.
VITE_LIVE_HOST_ORIGIN=

# LIVE mode only — the dev:live host NAV's Buzz balance. This is your PERSONAL
# API key (create at https://civitai.com/user/account). The nav's balance route is
# a signed-in-user route that does not accept a block token (the APP's balance
# read goes through the host bridge instead), so the dev:live nav reads your balance through the vite
# proxy, which injects THIS key as the Authorization header SERVER-SIDE on the
# `/api/trpc/buzz.getBuzzAccount` route only — it is NEVER bundled into client JS
# (that's why it has NO `VITE_` prefix: Vite only exposes `VITE_*` to the client).
#
# ⚠️ DEV-ONLY SECRET — put the real value in the git-ignored `.env.development.local`,
# NEVER here and NEVER committed. "NEVER here" is about the upload as much as
# git: `civitai app submit` ships this file (see VITE_LIVE_BLOCK_TOKEN above).
# Leaving it unset is fine: the nav then shows your profile name only (no
# balance), no error.
#   CIVITAI_HOST_KEY=<your-personal-api-key>   # in .env.development.local only
CIVITAI_HOST_KEY=
